{"author":"Unknown","author_email":"","data":{"content_hash":"f77a497084d6885a41146fefecd39678f66da45c29d446338ef83ada4f70a984","digest":{"component_or_area":"CI/documentation validation","key_entities":["README.md",".github/workflows/test.yml",".github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml","scripts/check_readme_quickstart.sh","scripts/check_readme_quickstart.py","scripts/probe-rebar.sh","rebar init","rebar create","rebar ready","rebar claim","rebar close","session-log","pipx","pip install"],"problem_keywords":["readme quickstart","ci gating","command drift","documentation correctness","golden path probe","end-to-end verification","packaging regression","cli invocation","stale documentation"],"propositions":["A CI job must extract the fenced bash quickstart block from README.md and execute those exact lines end-to-end in an isolated environment to catch wrong commands, missing verbs, stale hard-coded ids, or invocation errors printed in documentation.","The golden-path CI job must run against a clean, non-editable install (pip install . from a built wheel) to detect packaging and entry-point regressions that an editable install cannot catch.","Wrong text printed in the README quickstart — such as session-log missing its append verb or incorrect arguments — must cause the CI job to fail the build with a non-zero exit code.","The extracted README text itself must be what executes, not an independent probe script, to ensure the literal printed commands are correct.","The golden-path job must cover the init→create→ready→claim→close workflow subset as the primary gating check while retaining probe-rebar.sh as complementary coverage."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b2b5c498-2f67-4ae3-bafc-eca40294bec2","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1785817712170944304,"uuid":"bae428dd-a373-496b-b247-b1e79a2581a5"}